hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24188","Husayn, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, al-Fudayl, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Khunays al-Ghifari, from Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: Between Kada and Uhud is inviolable; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made it inviolable. I would not cut a tree in it nor kill a bird in it."
"24189","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, al-Dahhak narrated to me, from Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: I said, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sitting: We find in Allah's book, on Friday an hour no Muslim servant coincides with while he is in prayer and asks Allah, Mighty and Majestic, something but He gives him what he asked. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gestured saying: Part of an hour. He said: I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told the truth. Abu al-Nadr said: Abu Salamah said: I asked him which hour it is. He said: The last hours of the day. I said: It is not a prayer hour. He said: Yes, the Muslim servant is in his prayer when he prays then sits in his prayer place, nothing detains him but waiting for prayer."
"24190","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yala Abu Muhayyah al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, the son of Abdullah ibn Salam's brother narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and my name was not Abdullah ibn Salam, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named me Abdullah ibn Salam."
"24191","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Awf, Zurarah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salam said; and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Zurarah, from Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah, people rushed to him, and I was among those who rushed. When I discerned his face I knew that his face is not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him say was: Spread peace, feed food, join wombs, and pray while people sleep, you will enter Paradise in peace."
"24192","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Then I met Abdullah ibn Salam, then he mentioned the hadith. Then Abdullah ibn Salam said: I have known which hour it is. Abu Hurayrah said: I said to him: Tell me and do not withhold from me. Abdullah said: It is the last hour of Friday. Abu Hurayrah said: How can it be the last hour of Friday when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim servant praying coincides with it, and that is an hour in which prayer is not performed? Abdullah ibn Salam said: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, not say: Whoever sits a sitting waiting in it for prayer is in prayer until he prays? I said: Yes. He said: It is that."
"24193","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Then I met Abdullah ibn Salam, then he mentioned the hadith. Then Abdullah ibn Salam said: I have known which hour it is. Abu Hurayrah said: I said to him: Tell me and do not withhold from me. Abdullah said: It is the last hour of Friday. Abu Hurayrah said: How can it be the last hour of Friday when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim servant praying coincides with it, and that is an hour in which prayer is not performed? Abdullah ibn Salam said: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, not say: Whoever sits a sitting waiting in it for prayer is in prayer until he prays? I said: Yes. He said: It is that."
"24194","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Then I met Abdullah ibn Salam, then he mentioned the hadith. Then Abdullah ibn Salam said: I have known which hour it is. Abu Hurayrah said: I said to him: Tell me and do not withhold from me. Abdullah said: It is the last hour of Friday. Abu Hurayrah said: How can it be the last hour of Friday when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim servant praying coincides with it, and that is an hour in which prayer is not performed? Abdullah ibn Salam said: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, not say: Whoever sits a sitting waiting in it for prayer is in prayer until he prays? I said: Yes. He said: It is that."
"24195","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I met Abdullah ibn Salam and told him my hadith and the hadith of Kab about his saying in every year. He said: Kab lied; it is as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, in every Friday. I said: He has returned. He said: By the One in whose hand is Abdullah ibn Salam's soul, I know that hour. He said: I said: O Abdullah, tell me of it. He said: It is the last hour of Friday. He said: I said: He said: No believer coincides while praying. He said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever waits for prayer is in prayer until he prays? I said: Yes. He said: It is like that."
"24196","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Qays ibn Abbad, he said: I was in the mosque, and a man came in whose face was a trace of humility. He entered and prayed two rakahs, shortening in them. The people said: This is a man of the people of Paradise. When he went out I followed him until he entered his house, and I entered with him and talked to him. When he became familiar I said to him: The people when you entered before the mosque said such and such. He said: Glory be to Allah, it is not proper for anyone to say what he does not know. I will tell you why: I saw a dream in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told it to him. I saw as if I were in a green garden. Ibn Awn said: He mentioned of its greenness and expanse, in its middle an iron pillar, its bottom in the earth and its top in the heaven, at its top a handhold. It was said to me: Climb it. I said: I cannot. A servant came to me. Ibn Awn said: He is the attendant. He lifted my clothes from behind me and said: Climb it. I climbed until I took the handhold. He said: Hold to the handhold. I awoke and it was in my hand. He said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told it to him. He said: As for the garden, it is the garden of Islam; as for the pillar, it is the pillar of Islam; as for the handhold, it is the firmest handhold. You are upon Islam until you die. He said: He is Abdullah ibn Salam."
"24197","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah and from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: We mentioned which of you will come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ask him which deeds are most beloved to Allah Almighty. None of us stood, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a man to us and gathered us, and recited to us this surah, meaning the surah of al-Saff, all of it."
"24198","Yaamar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, al-Awzai informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to me that Ata ibn Yasar narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Salam narrated to him, or he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: We mentioned among us and said: Which of you will come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ask him which deeds are most beloved to Allah, and we feared that any of us stand. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to us a man, a man, until he gathered us. Some of us began pointing to others. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited to us: Glorified Allah what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, to His saying: Greatly hateful with Allah. He said: He recited it from its first to its last. He said: Ibn Salam recited it to us from its first to its last. He said: Ata ibn Yasar recited it to us from its first to its last. Yahya said: Hilal recited it to us from its first to its last. Al-Awzai said: Yahya recited it to us from its first to its last."
"24199","Yaamar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, al-Awzai informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to me that Ata ibn Yasar narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Salam narrated to him, or he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: We mentioned among us and said: Which of you will come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ask him which deeds are most beloved to Allah, and we feared that any of us stand. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to us a man, a man, until he gathered us. Some of us began pointing to others. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited to us: Glorified Allah what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, to His saying: Greatly hateful with Allah. He said: He recited it from its first to its last. He said: Ibn Salam recited it to us from its first to its last. He said: Ata ibn Yasar recited it to us from its first to its last. Yahya said: Hilal recited it to us from its first to its last. Al-Awzai said: Yahya recited it to us from its first to its last."
"24200","Hasan ibn Musa and Affan said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, he said: I came to Madinah and sat with elders in the mosque of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. An old man came leaning on a staff of his. The people said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at this. He stood behind a pillar and prayed two rakahs. I stood to him and said to him, some of the people said such and such. He said: Paradise belongs to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He enters into it whom He wills. I saw in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a dream: I saw as if a man came to me and said: Set out. I went with him, and he took me by a great path. A road presented to me on my left, and I wanted to take it. He said: You are not of its people. Then a road presented to me on my right, and I took it until I ended at a slippery mountain. He took my hand and pushed me, and I was upon its peak, neither settling nor holding. There was an iron pillar at its peak with a gold ring. He took my hand and pushed me until I took the handhold. He said: Hold. I said: Yes. He struck the pillar with his foot, and I held to the handhold. I told it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: You saw good. As for the great path, it is the gathering; as for the road that presented on your left, it is the road of the people of Fire, and you are not of its people; as for the road that presented on your right, it is the road of the people of Paradise; as for the slippery mountain, it is the station of the martyrs; as for the handhold you held to, it is the handhold of Islam, so hold to it until you die. He said: I hope to be of the people of Paradise. He said: He is Abdullah ibn Salam."
"24201","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I came to Sham and met Ka'b, and he would narrate to me from the Torah while I would narrate to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until we came to mention Friday, so I told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Friday there is an hour no Muslim coincides with it asking Allah for good therein except He gives it to him. So Ka'b said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; it is once every year. I said: No. So Ka'b looked for a while, then said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; it is once every month. I said: No. So he looked for a while and said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; in every Friday once. I said: Yes. So Ka'b said: Do you know which day it is? I said: And which day is it? He said: In it Allah created Adam, and in it the Hour will come, and the creatures in it are listening attentively except the two heavy ones, the jinn and mankind, out of fear of the Resurrection. So I came to Madinah and informed Abdullah ibn Salam of Ka'b's saying, and he said: Ka'b has lied. I said: He has returned to my saying. So he said: Do you know which hour it is? I said: No, and I pressed him insistently: Tell me, tell me. So he said: It is between al-Asr and al-Maghrib. I said: How, when there is no prayer? He said: Did you not hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The servant remains in prayer so long as he is in his prayer place waiting for the prayer."
